e's data location is pending; Priya Nair cited this as the reason for deferring the final call to 21 October.\n- Build cost for Option B has not been put on the table; raised by Dev Raman.\n\n## Next steps\n- Carla Mendes asked Clauseline for a written quote by Oct 14 (quote since received at $54k/year).\n- Priya Nair asked Carla Mendes to still get the quote despite the security review being outstanding.\n- Ines Duarte asked Priya Nair to own the 15 November contract signing deadline.\n- Dev Raman asked for the build cost for Option B to be formally considered.\n\n## Awaiting a reply\n- Priya Nair asked all participants to share their views by Thursday; no reply recorded from Jun Okafor on the option preference (seen by full audience).\n\n## Things people asserted that others may want to check\n- Tom Whitfield said Legal reviews approximately 40 vendor contracts a month and that redline turnaround is the biggest delay.\n- Tom Whitfield said Clauseline claims a 2-day redline turnaround.\n- Dev Raman said Option B would need two engineers for eight weeks.\n- Carla Mendes said the Clauseline quote is $54,000 a year on a three-year term, within her $60,000 cap.\n\n## Marked private\n- Marked private by Jun Okafor: Clauseline's documentation indicates contracts are processed in an EU region.\n- Marked private by Jun Okafor: A company rule requires vendor contract text to stay in the US.\n- Marked private by Jun Okafor: Clauseline's SOC 2 report is under review; Jun expects it by 21 October."
